---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Personal Chief of Staff | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A local-first, multi-agent personal assistant using LangGraph and read-only MCP servers for calendar, email, tasks, and meeting preparation."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>OPEN-SOURCE PROJECT · LANGGRAPH · MCP</p>
			<h1>Personal Chief of Staff</h1>
			<p>
				A local-first assistant for daily briefings, email triage,
				meeting preparation, and scheduling suggestions. A LangGraph
				supervisor routes each request to a focused specialist that
				uses only the read-only MCP tools you configure.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="architecture">
				<h2 id="architecture">A supervisor, four specialists</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Scheduler:</strong> finds candidate openings without changing the calendar.</li>
					<li><strong>Email Triager:</strong> prioritizes messages and drafts replies without sending.</li>
					<li><strong>Meeting Prep:</strong> gathers relevant context and flags gaps before a call.</li>
					<li><strong>Daily Briefing:</strong> summarizes calendar, inbox, and tasks into an actionable overview.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Connect trusted stdio MCP servers for Google Calendar,
					Gmail, Notion or Todoist, Slack, or search. Tool access
					fails closed: only explicitly read-only or recognizable
					read tools are included in the agent graph.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="demo">
				<h2 id="demo">Try it with synthetic data</h2>
				<pre><code>cd personal-chief-of-staff
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
chief-of-staff run "Give me my daily briefing"
chief-of-staff web</code></pre>
				<p>
					Demo mode needs no API key, makes no external calls, and
					uses clearly labeled sample data. The FastAPI interface
					runs locally at <code>127.0.0.1:8787</code>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Live mode requires your own trusted MCP servers and model
					credentials. Retrieved information is sent to the model
					provider you configure. This starter does not store
					requests or results.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="code">
				<h2 id="code">Explore the project</h2>
				<p>
					Read the setup, architecture, MCP configuration, safety
					boundaries, and example workflows in the
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/my_research_work"
						>project README</a
					>.
				</p>
				<p><a href="/projects/benchmarkkit">Explore BenchmarkKit</a> · <a href="/">Back to profile</a></p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
